# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  WHAT THE IMAGE DOES NOT NEED — which is nearly everything.
#
#  `docker build .` sends the whole context to the daemon before it
#  executes a single instruction. Without this file that is 2.1 GB, of
#  which the image copies 590 MB and uses none of the rest:
#
#      node_modules   811 MB   the build already ran, in CI
#      .next          620 MB   intermediate output; `out/` is the artifact
#      .git            54 MB
#      public          15 MB   already inlined into out/ by the export
#
#  The first production push spent over twenty minutes on this step. The
#  image is nginx plus a static directory; it has no use for a toolchain.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

node_modules
.next
.git
.github
.data-snapshot
.claude

# Sources and tooling — the export is prebuilt in CI and copied in whole.
src
tests
scripts
supabase
db3d
public
deploy/*.md
*.md
package*.json
tsconfig.json
next.config.*
eslint.config.*
postcss.config.*

# Local noise
.env*
.DS_Store
*.log
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
